e16ob11re7pdf01.pdf"}], "type": "question"}]}], "type": "DWS", "id": 11, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Write a dialogue about what you want to plan for your holidays."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn6le16ob11re2img06.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn6le16ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn6le16ob11re2img06.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn6le16ob11re2img06.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: This party was great! Everyone had so much fun. The best part is that we have all this food left.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Look at the state of the dining room! It's a mess. There are plates and glasses everywhere. It's going to take a while to clean it all up.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Don't worry, V. I will help you with that."}, {"time": "16150", "image": "engenn6le16ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh thanks, Sally. You're the best. Why don't you start with the kitchen?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I think I'd rather stick to the living room. I don't want to mess with your utensils! Besides, there is plenty to do around here, don't you think?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Alright. You should start by collecting all the empty jars and tins.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Sure. I'm picking up the trays after that. We'll put the leftovers in the fridge."}, {"time": "36250", "image": "engenn6le16ob11re2img06.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I'm not sure there is space in there. There are a couple of gallons of juice and a quart of gravy. Honestly, having parties at home is exhausting.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Well, we should get started then! I think we deserve a good night's sleep too. Besides, my interview with Luther is tomorrow at 10 ..."}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa and Sally Plan a Party"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Cleaning Up"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe  routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le16ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About Future Actions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use four different tenses to talk about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>When you talk about a things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>.</li>  <li>When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">going to</span>.</li>  <li>When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense.</li>  <li>When you talk about schedules or timetables in the future, you use the Simple Present tense</li></ul>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Will</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I will help you with that. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Going to </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's going to take a while to clean it all up. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Present Continuous</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I'm picking up the trays after that. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">  Simple Present tense</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"My interview is tomorrow at 10.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Respond Politely to Suggestions and Offers"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When someone offers suggestions, it is important to respond politely<br><br>Remember to use the modals <span class=\"italic\">could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should</span> or <span class=\"italic\">might</span> to suggest something."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here is a list of expressions you can use to give suggestions:<br>  <ul><li>You might want to \u2026</li> <li>Would you mind \u2026 ?</li> <li>You should \u2026</li> <li>You ought to \u2026 (strong request)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Offering Suggestions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Responding to Offers and Suggestions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>Would you like\u2026?</li><li>Can I get you \u2026 ?</li><li>Would you mind \u2026 ?</li><li>Why don't ...</li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>I don't think I can \u2026</li> <li>I guess that could ...</li> <li>That would be \u2026</li> <li>I would \u2026</li> <li>I think I'd rather ...</li></ul>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: Why don't you start with the kitchen?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>:  I think I'd rather stick to the living room."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "jar "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a wide-mouthed cylindrical container made of glass "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to buy a jar of pickles."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le16ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words to review."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tin "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a metal container "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I need to get a couple of tins of capers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le16ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " gallon "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a measuring unit for liquids equal to four quarts (3.5 liters) "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's buy a gallon of orange juice."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le16ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tray "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large serving dish "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'll prepare a tray of hors d'oeuvres."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le16ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "leftovers "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " food left after a meal "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The best part is that you'll have leftovers for days!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le16ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "exhausting "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "tiring "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Playing gigs all time sounds exhausting!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le16ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gravy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the fat and juices you get from meat after cooking"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: The gravy is not ready yet."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le16ob11aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue (12-14 lines) about your plans for the next holidays."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, think of 5 or 6 things to do. Make sure you include: <ul> <li>quantities and amounts</li> <li>actions in the future</li> </ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make suggestions and talk about preferences. Express your disagreement about the activities and respond politely."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find one suggestion that you both agree on."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your dialogue aloud."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I make suggestions and respond to offers."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a dialogue and read it aloud."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about what I plan to do in the future."}]}]}